  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case feature sample retains 20 failures and is not a global compatibility percentage.",
    "Renaming covers admitted single-column immediate NO ACTION declarations. Table/composite REFERENCES, deferred constraints, other actions and legacy_alter_table modes remain limited.",
    "The lexical no-target and unrelated-statement contracts are component proofs; catalog retention separately validates schema equality. These do not prove complete SQLite rename equivalence or all storage effects.",
    "Views, triggers and other unadmitted schema objects do not yet participate in rename propagation. Parent matching still uses supported affinities and BINARY comparison.",
    "Existing SQL/schema/storage and concurrency limitations remain. The 60 SIGKILL samples cover earlier storage paths rather than all rename failure schedules."
  ],
